<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-22T01:44:37+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:44:37 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[RSS-affiliated labour organisation opens first Kashmir office in Pulwama]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rss-affiliated-labour-organisation-opens-first-kashmir-office-in-pulwama/articleshow/135099884.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135099884.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[BMS has been actively working in Kashmir since 2020 after the abrogation of Article 370 and currently has 20 registered affiliated labour unions in the region, Khuchay said. Initially, there were a lot of misconceptions about RSS, he said. However, the BMS functionary claimed that over the years, he had succeeded in convincing the people that RSS was not anti-Muslim, but pro-labour and pro-people.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rss-affiliated-labour-organisation-opens-first-kashmir-office-in-pulwama/articleshow/135099884.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rss-affiliated-labour-organisation-opens-first-kashmir-office-in-pulwama/articleshow/135099884.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T00:57:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135100055,imgsize-46697.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Drone-linked narco-terror module busted in Jammu; 804 gm heroin; 1.1 kg opium seized]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drone-linked-narco-terror-module-busted-in-jammu-804-gm-heroin-1-1-kg-opium-seized/articleshow/135099887.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135099887.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[“Preliminary investigation has indicated a cross-border nexus. Inquiry is underway to identify the source of the consignment, its intended recipients, and persons involved in the network,” police said. The network came to light during the questioning of a 26-year-old man arrested for consuming drugs in RS Pura on Wednesday. Police said, “The arrested man, Sunny Kumar, a resident of Kotli Mirdian, Suchetgarh, revealed about the smuggling module.”]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drone-linked-narco-terror-module-busted-in-jammu-804-gm-heroin-1-1-kg-opium-seized/articleshow/135099887.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drone-linked-narco-terror-module-busted-in-jammu-804-gm-heroin-1-1-kg-opium-seized/articleshow/135099887.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T00:48:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sanjay Khajuria</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135099978,imgsize-151720.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who are the terrorists? J&amp;K and Ladakh high court questions ‘vague’ detention order]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-are-the-terrorists-jk-and-ladakh-high-court-questions-vague-detention-order/articleshow/135099891.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135099891.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A single bench of Justice Wasim Nargal said preventive detention, which allows authorities to deprive a person of liberty without a regular criminal trial, demands the “highest degree of constitutional responsibility and procedural diligence”. The court directed the DC to appear with the detention order, police dossier, material placed before him and records showing his consideration of the case and subjective satisfaction before ordering detention under PSA.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-are-the-terrorists-jk-and-ladakh-high-court-questions-vague-detention-order/articleshow/135099891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-are-the-terrorists-jk-and-ladakh-high-court-questions-vague-detention-order/articleshow/135099891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T00:46:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135099948,imgsize-1238902.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Congress pulls up SBI over data breach, seeks accountability; experts call leak 'no ordinary incident']]></title><description><![CDATA[Congress has raised concerns regarding a significant data exposure involving 3,897 customer records from State Bank of India. The bank confirmed the leak following alerts from its cybersecurity providers and has since initiated an investigation. Experts warned that the leaked data may pose risks to national security due to the bank's prominence. Meanwhile, SBI assured that customer balances remain safe and are implementing security measures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-pulls-up-sbi-over-data-breach-seeks-accountability-experts-call-leak-no-ordinary-incident/articleshow/135097889.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-pulls-up-sbi-over-data-breach-seeks-accountability-experts-call-leak-no-ordinary-incident/articleshow/135097889.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T23:27:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135098110,imgsize-109586.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7,000 people from 126 districts once hit by Naxalism to attend Ekta Diwas parade in Kevadia]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/7000-people-from-126-districts-once-hit-by-naxalism-to-attend-ekta-diwas-parade-in-kevadia/articleshow/135097872.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135097872.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/7000-people-from-126-districts-once-hit-by-naxalism-to-attend-ekta-diwas-parade-in-kevadia/articleshow/135097872.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/7000-people-from-126-districts-once-hit-by-naxalism-to-attend-ekta-diwas-parade-in-kevadia/articleshow/135097872.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T23:17:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135097927,imgsize-33360.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ankita Bhandari case: CBI serves notice to actress Urmila Sanawar for narco test]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ankita-bhandari-case-cbi-serves-notice-to-actress-urmila-sanawar-for-narco-test/articleshow/135097934.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135097934.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ankita-bhandari-case-cbi-serves-notice-to-actress-urmila-sanawar-for-narco-test/articleshow/135097934.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ankita-bhandari-case-cbi-serves-notice-to-actress-urmila-sanawar-for-narco-test/articleshow/135097934.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T23:16:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135097967,imgsize-109776.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Remain vigilant’: India urges citizens in France to avoid protest sites ahead of fresh demonstrations]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-vigilant-india-urges-citizens-in-france-to-avoid-protest-sites-ahead-of-fresh-demonstrations/articleshow/135097622.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135097622.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Indian Embassy in France has raised an alert for Indian nationals amid ongoing protests in the nation. Citizens are advised to avoid large gatherings and comply with directives from local officials. With violent outbreaks and curfews emerging in reaction to increasing living expenses, the French government braces for more unrest. Indians living in France should closely follow news updates and keep emergency contacts easily available.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-vigilant-india-urges-citizens-in-france-to-avoid-protest-sites-ahead-of-fresh-demonstrations/articleshow/135097622.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/remain-vigilant-india-urges-citizens-in-france-to-avoid-protest-sites-ahead-of-fresh-demonstrations/articleshow/135097622.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T23:09:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135097832,imgsize-143070.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India sees a drop in GHG emissions in 2025, even as UNEP flags huge gap in global reduction efforts]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-sees-a-drop-in-ghg-emissions-in-2025-even-as-unep-flags-huge-gap-in-global-reduction-efforts/articleshow/135096747.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135096747.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-sees-a-drop-in-ghg-emissions-in-2025-even-as-unep-flags-huge-gap-in-global-reduction-efforts/articleshow/135096747.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-sees-a-drop-in-ghg-emissions-in-2025-even-as-unep-flags-huge-gap-in-global-reduction-efforts/articleshow/135096747.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T22:24:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishwa Mohan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135096916,imgsize-850235.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Watch: 'Inquilab Zindabad', CJP leaders Saurav Das &amp; Ashutosh Ranka come out of Tihar Jail]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-inquilab-zindabad-cjp-leaders-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka-come-out-of-tihar-jail/articleshow/135095842.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135095842.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[After a week in judicial custody, Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were granted release from Tihar Jail by a special executive magistrate court in Delhi. Das joyfully declared that truth has prevailed, while Ranka chanted a memorable revolutionary slogan. CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke recognized their leadership through social media, and their return has sparked celebrations among supporters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-inquilab-zindabad-cjp-leaders-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka-come-out-of-tihar-jail/articleshow/135095842.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-inquilab-zindabad-cjp-leaders-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka-come-out-of-tihar-jail/articleshow/135095842.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T21:29:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135096071,imgsize-1149318.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rs 50k bond, no Jantar Mantar protest call: What are the conditions of CJP leaders' release]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-50k-bond-no-jantar-mantar-protest-call-what-are-the-conditions-of-cjp-leaders-release/articleshow/135095991.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135095991.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-50k-bond-no-jantar-mantar-protest-call-what-are-the-conditions-of-cjp-leaders-release/articleshow/135095991.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-50k-bond-no-jantar-mantar-protest-call-what-are-the-conditions-of-cjp-leaders-release/articleshow/135095991.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T21:25:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135096025,imgsize-89544.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[AAIB asks Alliance Air to ‘strengthen simulator training’ for pilots in serious incident probe report]]></title><description><![CDATA[The Aircraft Accident Investigation Bureau has recommended enhanced simulator training for Alliance Air pilots after a serious incident. On October 8, 2024, an Alliance ATR undershot the runway at Bhubaneswar due to severe rain. Pilots struggled with communication and situational awareness, leading to complications during landing. The investigation noted contributing weather factors such as turbulence and low visibility.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aaib-asks-alliance-air-to-strengthen-simulator-training-for-pilots-in-serious-incident-probe-report/articleshow/135095712.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aaib-asks-alliance-air-to-strengthen-simulator-training-for-pilots-in-serious-incident-probe-report/articleshow/135095712.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-21T21:06:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Saurabh Sinha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135095767,imgsize-107168.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Shouldn't have come if unwell': Subodh Uniyal defends public reprimand of Daler Mehndi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shouldnt-have-come-if-unwell-subodh-uniyal-defends-public-reprimand-of-daler-mehndi/articleshow/135095325.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135095325.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesof